	<item>
		<title><![CDATA[Five Signals Your Business Is Ready to Scale]]></title>
		<link>https://example.com/five-signals-your-business-is-ready-to-scale/</link>
		<pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[admin]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://example.com/?p=1014</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Growth feels exciting until the processes that carried a ten-person team start to crack at thirty. The earliest signal is usually founder bottleneck: every decision still runs through one person.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Second, look at delivery quality. When rework rises and onboarding drags, you are scaling revenue faster than capability. That is the moment to invest in systems, documentation and a leadership layer.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Finally, measure customer concentration and cash runway. Healthy scale means diversified revenue and enough runway to hire ahead of demand.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

]]></content:encoded>
		<excerpt:encoded><![CDATA[How to tell when growth needs structure, not just more effort.]]></excerpt:encoded>
